{"title":"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two nonadjacent vertices of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/563948106c3332662355412547d99acab218c16f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d653d09b4a98dcd868612d2e300e6fa7fd1173b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-4,-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Coordinate\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Coordinate\">coordinates</a> of the other two vertices are integers. The number of such rectangles is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235bf0fb4fe95fa381a39dd78e41a513ae19e1ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ 1 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ 2 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ 3 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ 4 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ 5 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The center of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, and the distance from the center to a corner is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fbf23462b7dfe6f9e220bc085774f2f1b5738dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{4^2+3^2}=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />. The remaining two vertices of the rectangle must be another pair of points opposite each other on the circle of radius 5 centered at the origin. Let these points have the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/40554563bdf15630c43a351a54067b29847cbdf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pm x,\\pm y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/4/b44d73f837d8bbe7098c2c2bcbd6facc4d61bd0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />. This equation has six pairs of integer solutions: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f3130a4f1f8e73f4db6bd08c633f60a0f5d0f60a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pm 4, \\pm 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a81f5a704dc9ae61f4e8d2da53dc95bab3a2f492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pm 4, \\mp 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d210d051d65fd55e216c4ab8b9035ad1de70b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pm 3, \\pm 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90f8e4880416bfe2b607b541a512d12ab69455a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pm 3, \\mp 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/85664b0f112bba12f85b0935f472343a9e6fb611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pm 5, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a49e9c1bc6471eed8b47eea8e03893a82edf579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, \\pm 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />. The first pair of solutions are the endpoints of the given diagonal, and the other diagonal must span one of the other five pairs of points. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598c140dd07a9e2359d2a073257ea27b86f9bfdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME\" title=\"1995 AHSME\">1995 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1995 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Prob